 234:./ucos/Core/os_dbg_r.c **** /*
 235:./ucos/Core/os_dbg_r.c **** ***************************************************************************************************
 236:./ucos/Core/os_dbg_r.c **** *                                       OS DEBUG INITIALIZATION
 237:./ucos/Core/os_dbg_r.c **** *
 238:./ucos/Core/os_dbg_r.c **** * Description: This function is used to make sure that debug variables that are unused in the appli
 239:./ucos/Core/os_dbg_r.c **** *              are not optimized away.  This function might not be necessary for all compilers.  In
 240:./ucos/Core/os_dbg_r.c **** *              case, you should simply DELETE the code in this function while still leaving the dec
 241:./ucos/Core/os_dbg_r.c **** *              of the function itself.
 242:./ucos/Core/os_dbg_r.c **** *
 243:./ucos/Core/os_dbg_r.c **** * Arguments  : none
 244:./ucos/Core/os_dbg_r.c **** *
 245:./ucos/Core/os_dbg_r.c **** * Returns    : none
 246:./ucos/Core/os_dbg_r.c **** *
 247:./ucos/Core/os_dbg_r.c **** * Note(s)    : (1) This code doesn't do anything, it simply prevents the compiler from optimizing o
 248:./ucos/Core/os_dbg_r.c **** *                  the 'const' variables which are declared in this file.
 249:./ucos/Core/os_dbg_r.c **** *              (2) You may decide to 'compile out' the code (by using #if 0/#endif) INSIDE the func
 250:./ucos/Core/os_dbg_r.c **** *                  if your compiler DOES NOT optimize out the 'const' variables above.
 251:./ucos/Core/os_dbg_r.c **** ***************************************************************************************************
 252:./ucos/Core/os_dbg_r.c **** */
 253:./ucos/Core/os_dbg_r.c **** 
